/* Mouse Click Support
Reference: &mkp
|  ---------  |  ---------------|
|  MB1, LCLK  |  Left click     |
|  MB2, RCLK  |  Right click    |
|  MB3, MCLK  |  Middle click   |
|  MB4        |  Mouse button 4 |
|  MB5        |  Mouse button 5 |
*/

/* Mouse Move Support
Reference: &mmv
|  ---         |  ---         |
|  MOVE_UP     |  Move up     |
|  MOVE_DOWN   |  Move down   |
|  MOVE_LEFT   |  Move left   |
|  MOVE_RIGHT  |  Move right  |
Additionally, if you want to pass a different max speed than the
default for the MOVE_* defines, custom X and Y velocity values can be passed
with MOVE_X and MOVE_Y, e.g. MOVE_X(100) or MOVE_Y(-100). Positive values
indicate movement directions right or down. Note that the default value
of the max speed depends on the value of ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_MOVE_VAL.
*/

/* Mouse Scroll Support
Reference: &msc
SCRL_UP	Scroll up
SCRL_DOWN	Scroll down
SCRL_LEFT	Scroll left
SCRL_RIGHT	Scroll right
Additionally, if you want to pass a different max speed than the default
for the SCRL_* defines, custom X and Y velocity values can be passed
with MOVE_X and MOVE_Y, e.g. MOVE_X(5) or MOVE_Y(-5). Positive values
indicate scroll directions right or up. Note that the default value of
the max speed depends on the value of ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_SCRL_VAL.
*/

/*
Should you wish to override the default movement or scrolling max velocities,
you must define the defaults BEFORE including the header
*/
#define ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_MOVE_VAL 1100  // default: 600
#define ZMK_POINTING_DEFAULT_SCRL_VAL 15    // default: 10

